Subject: Reproduce the release versioning and package layout

Upstream's release script replaces stale assembly-version defaults and fills
in the package version. Set those values to match the official 9.0.1 package.
List the seven rebuilt assemblies and their XML documentation explicitly so
dotnet pack can assemble the package using upstream's existing dependency groups.

diff --git a/Build/Newtonsoft.Json.nuspec b/Build/Newtonsoft.Json.nuspec
index e5418d7b..830bd754 100644
--- a/Build/Newtonsoft.Json.nuspec
+++ b/Build/Newtonsoft.Json.nuspec
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 <package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2010/07/nuspec.xsd">
     <metadata>
         <id>Newtonsoft.Json</id>
-        <version></version>
+        <version>9.0.1</version>
         <title>Json.NET</title>
         <description>Json.NET is a popular high-performance JSON framework for .NET</description>
         <authors>James Newton-King</authors>
@@ -44,4 +44,20 @@
